1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,320
Welcome to this podcast about the Sheep market

2
00:00:04,580 --> 00:00:07,090
which is one of the oldest parts of the city.

3
00:00:07,090 --> 00:00:10,500
As its name suggests, there was originally a market here

4
00:00:10,500 --> 00:00:12,036
where farmers brought their sheep,

5
00:00:12,036 --> 00:00:14,674
but now it's been redeveloped into a buzzing,

6
00:00:14,674 --> 00:00:16,280
vibrant area of the city

7
00:00:16,280 --> 00:00:19,950
which is also home to one of the city's fastest-growing communities.

8
00:00:19,950 --> 00:00:23,522
The nearby university has always meant the area's popular with students,

9
00:00:23,522 --> 00:00:26,160
who come in to enjoy the lively nightlife

10
00:00:26,500 --> 00:00:29,692
but now graduates embarking on careers in the worlds of fashion

11
00:00:29,692 --> 00:00:35,000
and design are buying up the new apartments recently built here to replace the small houses

12
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:37,160
where the market workers used to live.

13
00:00:37,160 --> 00:00:41,530
The narrow old side streets are great places for finding original pictures,

14
00:00:41,530 --> 00:00:44,160
jewellery and ceramics which won't break the bank

15
00:00:44,220 --> 00:00:47,720
as well as local produce like fruit and vegetables.

16
00:00:47,720 --> 00:00:51,047
There's also lots of pavement cafes where you can have a coffee

17
00:00:51,047 --> 00:00:53,820
and watch tourists from all over the world go by.

18
00:00:53,820 --> 00:00:57,628
The oldest buildings in the area are on the main streets,

19
00:00:57,628 --> 00:00:59,460
including the city's first department store

20
00:00:59,700 --> 00:01:02,820
built in the 1880s, which is still open today.

21
00:01:02,820 --> 00:01:05,440
The Sheep market is a centre for fashion

22
00:01:05,500 --> 00:01:08,980
and there's a policy of encouraging new young designers.

23
00:01:08,980 --> 00:01:12,500
The Young Fashion competition is open to local young people

24
00:01:12,500 --> 00:01:14,400
who are passionate about fashion.

25
00:01:14,400 --> 00:01:19,531
This year they've been asked to design an outfit based on the ideas from the music

26
00:01:19,531 --> 00:01:21,040
and technology that's part of their everyday life

27
00:01:21,040 --> 00:01:24,020
using both natural and man-made fibres.

28
00:01:24,020 --> 00:01:27,899
The garments will be judged by a panel of experts and fashion designers,

29
00:01:27,899 --> 00:01:31,480
and the winning entries will be modelled at a special gala evening.

30
00:01:31,480 --> 00:01:33,239
Parking at the Sheep market is easy.

31
00:01:33,239 --> 00:01:34,495
There are plenty of pay

32
00:01:34,495 --> 00:01:37,520
and display car parking spaces on the roadsides

33
00:01:37,760 --> 00:01:40,024
which are fine if you just want to stay for an hour or two,

34
00:01:40,024 --> 00:01:41,760
but if you want to spend the day there

35
00:01:41,760 --> 00:01:45,050
it's better to park in one of the four underground car parks.

36
00:01:45,050 --> 00:01:49,400
It's not expensive and if you can present a receipt from one of the local stores

37
00:01:49,420 --> 00:01:51,200
you'll not be charged at all.

38
00:01:51,200 --> 00:01:55,380
After six pm many of the car parks have a flat rate which varies

39
00:01:55,460 --> 00:01:57,700
but it is usually very reasonable.

40
00:01:57,700 --> 00:02:00,620
The Sheep market is one of the main centres for art

41
00:02:00,620 --> 00:02:02,780
and history in the whole of the country.

42
00:02:02,780 --> 00:02:06,840
If you look at our map, you'll see some of the main attractions there.

43
00:02:06,840 --> 00:02:10,320
Most visitors start from Crawley Road, at the bottom of the map.

44
00:02:10,320 --> 00:02:13,800
The Reynolds House is one of the oldest houses in the city

45
00:02:13,800 --> 00:02:15,520
and is open to the public.

46
00:02:15,520 --> 00:02:18,340
It's on the north side of Crawley Road

47
00:02:18,580 --> 00:02:21,950
next to the footpath that leads to the public gardens.

48
00:02:21,950 --> 00:02:24,983
The area's particularly interesting for its unusual sculptures.

49
00:02:24,983 --> 00:02:30,291
'The Thumb' is just what its name suggests, but it's about 10 metres high.

50
00:02:30,291 --> 00:02:34,840
You'll see it on Hill Road, across the road from the Bank.

51
00:02:34,840 --> 00:02:39,400
The Museum's got a particularly fine collection of New Zealand landscapes.

52
00:02:39,400 --> 00:02:43,523
It's on the east side of the Sheep market, on City Road.

53
00:02:43,523 --> 00:02:46,540
It's on the other side of the road from the public gardens

54
00:02:47,100 --> 00:02:50,050
immediately facing the junction with Hill Road.

55
00:02:50,050 --> 00:02:54,565
The Contemporary Art Gallery is on a little road that leads off Station Square,

56
00:02:54,565 --> 00:02:56,500
not far from the public gardens.

57
00:02:56,500 --> 00:02:59,960
The road ends at the gallery - it doesn't go anywhere else

58
00:03:00,420 --> 00:03:03,230
That's open every day except Mondays.

59
00:03:03,230 --> 00:03:06,022
The Warner Gallery specialises in 19th-century art.

60
00:03:06,022 --> 00:03:10,880
It's on City Road, near the junction with Crawley Road

61
00:03:10,880 --> 00:03:14,400
on the same side of the road as the public gardens.

62
00:03:14,400 --> 00:03:19,680
It's open on weekdays from 9 to 5, and entry is free.

63
00:03:19,680 --> 00:03:23,460
Finally, if you're interested in purchasing high quality artwork

64
00:03:24,020 --> 00:03:26,280
the place to go is Nucleus.

65
00:03:26,280 --> 00:03:29,990
You need to go from Crawley Road up through Station Square

66
00:03:29,990 --> 00:03:35,050
and east along Hill Road until you get to a small winding road turning off.

67
00:03:35,050 --> 00:03:41,720
Go up there and it's on your right - if you get to City Road you've gone too far.
